## Summary

Store and cache failures arrive as emergencies: a disk fills mid-build, GC
deletes roots a fleet still needs, the cache-push queue pins at its limit
and starves, the daemon crashes under concurrent CA imports. Each incident
produced a watchdog or a recipe; none produced a lifecycle. This plan
manages the substrate as one loop per host: budgeted, checkpointed GC that
respects fleet-wide roots; push admission with backpressure that sheds load
instead of livelocking; and daemon health that reports to the same place
CI status does.

## Non-goals

Replacing the cache plane or the Nix fork; this manages what exists.

